This getter is already a single constant-argument typed-field lookup, so there is no safe transformation that avoids new calls or changes scale/offset rounding; I kept the exact call path to preserve bit-identical results.

```cpp
    FIT_FLOAT32 GetEnhancedAvgAltitude(void) const
    {
        return GetFieldFLOAT32Value(126, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```